Enable every message mask at start-up.

The initial state of the masks is DIAG_CTRL_MASK_INVALID, so when
diag_cntl_send_masks() pushes the masks to a freshly found peripheral it is
telling it "emit nothing". Without a client explicitly sending command 0x7D,
the modem never opens its log stream.

To debug the modem we need the stream from the very first moment, before any
client could have connected. So we start with everything enabled.

--- a/router/masks.c
+++ b/router/masks.c
@@ -258,6 +258,14 @@ int diag_masks_init()
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Start with all the masks enabled: the modem must emit its
+	 * log from boot, without waiting for a client to ask for it.
+	 */
+	diag_cmd_set_all_msg_mask(0xffffffff);
+	log_mask.status = DIAG_CTRL_MASK_ALL_ENABLED;
+	event_mask.status = DIAG_CTRL_MASK_ALL_ENABLED;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
